  "description": "Fast binary protocol converter: describe a frame with attributes on a POCO and convert raw bytes, for example from a hardware device or a socket, into an instance and back. Compiled accessors instead of reflection, so a 38 byte frame reads in 59 ns and writes in 56 ns, and nothing at all is allocated per message when you read into an instance you keep and write into a buffer you own. Little and big endian at the same speed, fields and properties, ReadOnlySpan and IBufferWriter overloads.",
